 "level_notes": {
  "1": "MIPS Technologies' architecture manuals are the definition; official download links have moved repeatedly, so copies hosted by universities are linked. Assembly syntax (pseudo-instructions, $reg names) is set by the MIPS assembler conventions followed by GNU as and SPIM.",
  "0": "SPIM and MARS are the teaching simulators; GNU as, LLVM and QEMU provide production assemblers and emulation."
 },
